            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Kannada for to destroy, then the Kannada for to disappear."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಕ್ರಮೇಣ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಕ್ರಮೇಣ — kramēṇa — \"gradually\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಕ್ರಮೇಣ ಹಳ್ಳಿ ಒಂದು ಪಟ್ಟಣವಾಯಿತು. kramēṇa haḷḷi ondu paṭṭaṇavāyitu. Gradually the village became a town."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A formal adverb; in talk people say ನಿಧಾನವಾಗಿ or ಸ್ವಲ್ಪ ಸ್ವಲ್ಪವಾಗಿ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಕ್ರಮೇಣ (kramēṇa) is borrowed from Sanskrit krameṇa, \"in regular course, gradually, by degrees\" (Monier-Williams), a case form of krama, \"a step, an order\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
