          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಘಟ್ಟ — ghaṭṭa — \"a turning point; a stage\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಆ ಪರೀಕ್ಷೆ ಅವಳ ಜೀವನದ ಮುಖ್ಯ ಘಟ್ಟ. ā parīkṣe avaḷa jīvanada mukhya ghaṭṭa. That exam is a turning point in her life."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Also a hill slope or a mountain pass: ಘಟ್ಟದ ದಾರಿ, a road over the hills."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಘಟ್ಟ (ghaṭṭa) matches Sanskrit ghaṭṭa, \"a landing place, a quay, a ferry\" (CDIAL 4414). CDIAL and DEDR 1147 both compare it with Dravidian words for a bank or a dam, such as Kannada gaṭṭu, so its first source is not settled; \"a slope\" and \"a stage\" are later senses."
            }
          ]
        },
